From 62e162003f49512ed9088ca46e50674a76f6dd24 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 19:01:18 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] feat(mcp): serve the MCP tool table live from inside the
 GUI

An opt-in server (--mcp-port <n> or CAMCRAFT_MCP_PORT; off by default)
listens on 127.0.0.1 only and carries the same newline-delimited JSON-RPC
`camcraft-cli mcp` speaks on stdio. A listener thread moves lines to the
UI thread over a channel (waking the idle loop with an empty winit user
event); the UI answers them in State::drain_actions through the new
app::mcp::answer_live seam, which runs the existing tool dispatch against
the window's own world (a shared flecs handle) and History (lent for the
call). An agent's step is therefore an entry on the app's History: the
browser shows it and Ctrl+Z undoes it like a user step. open_project is
refused in the live session (it would skip the unsaved-changes prompt).

`camcraft-cli mcp --connect <host:port>` bridges stdio to the live
session for MCP clients that launch stdio servers. The status strip shows
"MCP listening on 127.0.0.1:<port>" while the server runs; dropping the
inbox at shutdown stops and joins the listener thread.

Pinned by crates/app/tests/mcp_live.rs (seam + undo, loopback socket,
bridge, port flag) and the ui lib tests egui_app::tests::mcp_live.
Decisions in docs/decisions/183-mcp-live-gui.md.

Fixes #183

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
