From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 14:32:42 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] fix(mcp): the live listener serves JSON-RPC lines only -
 a browser POST is refused

Review of #474: any web page can POST to 127.0.0.1, and the listener
read each line as JSON-RPC, so the HTTP headers failed but the body ran
- a page could call save_project, post or export_tool_library with its
own paths. Every non-blank line must now open a JSON object or array;
anything else is refused (-32600) and the connection closed before a
line reaches the app. Reads are bounded to the cap as they happen and
writes time out, so a client can neither grow memory nor stall the
listener.

