Subject: [PATCH 3/4] feat(mcp): an idle live-session client is dropped after a
 timeout

The live listener serves one client at a time; a local client that
connected and sent nothing held the session until it hung up. Now a
client that sends no complete line for the idle window (5 minutes by
default; Inbox::listen_with_idle sets another, floored at the 50 ms
poll step) gets an MCP notifications/message saying why, is closed,
is logged by peer address ("client <peer> dropped: idle ..."), and the
next client is served. The clock resets after each answered line, so
the app's own answering time never counts. A newcomer does not
pre-empt a connected client before that.

Fixes #567

